  <main class="shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div><div class="eyebrow">NCAA evidence review · 04 November 2026</div><h1 id="page-title">Forecast quality.<br>Visible limits.</h1><p>Different objectives produce different leaders. Explore the probabilities, point errors and uncertainty behind a separately evaluated college basketball track.</p><div class="league-pill" id="league-label">__TITLE__</div></div><aside class="hero-aside"><strong>One cohort. A clear comparison.</strong><p>Historical results below describe development-exposed research. The current season must build its own record of saved, timestamped forecasts.</p><a href="../__SIBLING__/index.html" class="league-pill">Explore __SIBLING_LABEL__ →</a></aside></section>
    <div class="status-strip"><div><strong>Latest workflow completed with explicit coverage gaps.</strong><span id="attempt-summary"></span></div><a href="#execution">See the work ↓</a></div>

    <section class="section" id="execution" aria-labelledby="execution-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Latest measured execution</div><h2 id="execution-title">Completed work. Measured limits.</h2></div><p id="execution-intro"></p></div>
      <div class="run-metrics" id="run-metrics"></div>
      <div class="execution-grid"><article class="panel"><h3>Where the elapsed time went</h3><p class="subtle">Measured across both NCAA leagues. Waiting and fixture tests do not count as science.</p><div class="time-bar" id="time-bar" role="img"></div><div class="time-legend" id="time-legend"></div><p class="table-note" id="resource-note"></p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Stage evidence</h3><div class="data-scroll"><table class="phase-table"><caption id="stage-caption"></caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Elapsed</th></tr></thead><tbody id="phase-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note">All 12 workflow stages returned. A completed qualification stage can still reject an original model or defer a monitor. Workflow completion is not complete scientific acceptance.</p></article></div>
    </section>
    <div class="snapshot-note" id="preserved-study"><strong>Preserved B033 historical study</strong><span id="preserved-study-copy"></span><details style="margin-top:10px"><summary>Inspect the prior stage evidence</summary><div class="data-scroll"><table class="phase-table"><caption>Prior B033 stages; reused fits remain separate from new fits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Elapsed</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history-phase-table"></tbody></table></div></details></div>
    <section class="section" id="historical" aria-labelledby="historical-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Historical evidence</div><h2 id="historical-title">Choose the question first.</h2></div><p>The same pooled selection is shown in each season. A seasonal view changes the evaluation window; it does not choose a new winner.</p></div>
      <div class="filters"><label for="objective">Objective<select id="objective"><option value="probability">Win probability</option><option value="accuracy">Winner accuracy</option><option value="margin">Point margin</option><option value="total">Total points</option></select></label><label for="season">Evaluation window<select id="season"><option value="pooled">Both historical seasons</option><option value="2025">2024–25</option><option value="2026">2025–26</option></select></label><div class="selection-note" id="selection-note"></div></div>
      <div class="metrics" id="metrics" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <div class="chart-grid"><div class="panel"><h3 id="chart-title">Reliability, in ten bins.</h3><p class="subtle" id="chart-subtitle"></p><div id="chart"></div><div class="legend" id="chart-legend"></div><p class="table-note" id="chart-note"></p></div><div class="panel"><h3 id="table-title">Objective-specific selections</h3><p class="subtle">Public IDs preserve the result without exposing private model recipes.</p><div class="data-scroll"><table id="model-table"><caption id="table-caption"></caption><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note" id="table-note"></p></div></div>
      <p class="qualification">The two seasons selected these models after evaluation. They are development-exposed, retrospective comparisons. Historical feature releases use a declared 24-hour assumption; full official-season completeness and prospective performance are not established.</p>
      <div class="panel tradeoff" id="tradeoff"><div><div class="eyebrow">Probability versus accuracy</div><h3>Point estimates tell only part of the story.</h3><p>The probability selection is compared with the accuracy selection on identical games. Whole weeks are resampled within each season, 2,000 times. Intervals describe this exposed selection; they are not adjusted for model search.</p></div><div id="tradeoff-values"></div></div>
    </section>
    <div class="snapshot-note"><strong>Your complete private game report</strong><p>Open every supplied game, forecast reconstruction, captured price and unresolved market record in the browser-only viewer. Missing forecasts and quotes stay visible. The report file is never published or uploaded.</p><a class="league-pill" href="https://alvaro-ncaa-research-review.alv-mendizabal.chatgpt.site/private-report/index.html">Open private game report →</a></div>
    <section class="section" id="current" aria-labelledby="current-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / 2026–27 monitoring</div><h2 id="current-title">A new season needs new evidence.</h2></div><p>The latest run captured a larger current inventory and fitted chronological reconstructions. Original issues, eligible comparisons and exact official coverage remain separate requirements.</p></div><div class="snapshot-note"><strong id="inventory-age"></strong><span>These are fresh source candidates from the recorded capture, including unmatched official records. Possible cross-source duplicates remain visible; the count is not a reconciled official denominator.</span></div><div class="panel"><h3>Visible coverage, with its denominator</h3><div class="coverage-grid" id="coverage-counts"></div><p class="table-note" id="week-counts"></p><p class="table-note">Exact official coverage remains unverified. Unknown phase, opponent division and exact start times, along with possible duplicate records, need reconciliation. Missing model or quote evidence must not erase an observed game.</p></div><div class="track-grid" style="margin-top:18px"><article class="track"><span class="badge">PRESERVED · NOT REPLACED</span><h3>Original frozen models</h3><p>Parameters, selection and genuine historical forecast timestamps remain unchanged. The original native feature engine and unchanged weights produced reconstructions or previews for 1,322 games. They retain their actual computation clocks and receive no earlier issue credit.</p><div class="track-footer"><span>New issued rows: <strong>0</strong></span><span>Reconstruction metrics: <strong>separate below</strong></span></div></article><article class="track"><span class="badge">RECONSTRUCTED · NOT AS ISSUED</span><h3>Rolling chronological models</h3><p>Each training origin must exclude unreleased labels and later corrections. New predictions require information available one to two hours before tipoff. More data does not guarantee lower future loss.</p><div class="track-footer"><span>Both leagues: <strong>156 target + 48 scalar + 60 empirical fits</strong></span><span>Issued forecasts: <strong>0</strong></span></div></article></div>
      <div class="panel providers"><h3>Collect broadly. Compare at the right clock.</h3><div class="data-scroll"><table><caption>Latest display coverage and forecast-eligible comparison coverage are separate.</caption><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th class="provider-product">Product scope</th><th>Latest display</th><th>Eligible comparison</th></tr></thead><tbody id="provider-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="gap-note">A captured price can be displayed even when its game has no qualified model forecast. Latest captured pre-tip, latest observed, and forecast-cutoff prices remain distinct. A late or recovered display quote cannot become an earlier model input, issue or executable profit. No current-season market advantage or ROI is established here.</p></div>
      <div class="panel providers" id="current-paired-review"><h3>Current frozen-original reconstruction</h3><p class="subtle" id="current-paired-note"></p><div class="data-scroll" id="current-paired-table"></div><p class="gap-note" id="current-paired-disagreements"></p></div>
      <details class="source-details"><summary>What failed, what completed, and what remains preserved</summary><p>The earlier B033 attempt restored its parent, built historical features and completed all 108 registered target fits across the two leagues. A shared-summary selector then encountered a summary belonging to another project and stopped the current-source refresh. The incomplete refresh produced no fresh current-game or provider coverage. The committed historical artifacts and the verified return remain preserved.</p><p>B035 later stopped before science with 510 passed fixtures, three errors and one skip. B036 corrected that portability problem and completed the workflow. It still recorded 417 current boxscore normalization errors, exchange identity gaps, a Kalshi rate-limit halt, and no configured runtime historical-odds credential. The earlier B032 attempt had failed at the streaming-reader boundary with zero completed scientific stages. That failure remains in the evidence history. Its later durability verification did not add scientific credit. The B033 stream repair allowed real work to proceed; neither repair nor test success implies full coverage or a market advantage.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="engineering" aria-labelledby="engineering-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Inspect the engineering</div><h2 id="engineering-title">Move a clock. Watch the contract.</h2></div><p>This interaction uses invented inputs only. The executable Python example tests the same classes of failure without credentials, subscriptions or cloud access.</p></div><div class="engineering"><div class="panel"><h3>Information available before 16:00 UTC</h3><p class="subtle">Invented tipoff: 18:00 UTC · decision horizon: two hours.</p><div class="demo-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented contract scenarios"><button type="button" data-scenario="valid" aria-pressed="true">All inputs in time</button><button type="button" data-scenario="late_quote" aria-pressed="false">Late quote</button><button type="button" data-scenario="boundary_label" aria-pressed="false">Boundary label</button><button type="button" data-scenario="settlement" aria-pressed="false">Wrong settlement</button></div><div class="demo-clocks"><div><span>Latest training label</span><strong id="demo-label">15:00 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Quote available</span><strong id="demo-quote">15:55 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Feature available</span><strong>15:10 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Settlement scope</span><strong id="demo-settlement">Full game + overtime</strong></div></div><div class="demo-output" id="demo-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="table-note">Passing a comparison contract does not authorize a wager. The public payoff example separately requires explicit price and fee evidence and always emits zero orders.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Reproduce the review mechanism.</h3><p class="subtle">Python 3.11+ · standard library · deterministic invented data.</p><pre class="code">python examples/ncaa_review/contracts.py --demo
python examples/ncaa_review/progress.py
python -m unittest discover -s examples/ncaa_review -p 'test_*.py'
python examples/ncaa_review/build_dashboard.py --check</pre><ul class="checklist"><li>Reject future and exact-boundary training labels.</li><li>Pair each provider on the exact same games and products.</li><li>Keep frozen, reconstructed and issued tracks separate.</li><li>Preserve both winning and losing disagreements.</li><li>Verify complete streamed bytes and close the actual reader.</li></ul><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/main/examples/ncaa_review">Read the source, tests and methodology ↗</a></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="progress" aria-labelledby="progress-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / Invented progress contract</div><h2 id="progress-title">An estimate needs evidence.</h2></div><p>Switch the invented scenario to inspect counts and a measured phase ETA. This is a reproducible demonstration, not a connection to a running owner workload.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="demo-buttons progress-buttons" id="progress-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented progress scenarios"></div><div class="progress-demo-grid"><div><span class="progress-key">Durably completed units</span><div class="progress-count" id="progress-count"></div><div class="progress-track" id="progress-track" role="progressbar" aria-label="Invented task completion"><span id="progress-fill"></span></div><div class="progress-subline" id="progress-components"></div></div><div id="progress-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"><span class="progress-key">Estimated time remaining in this phase</span><div class="progress-eta" id="progress-eta"></div><div class="progress-range" id="progress-range"></div><div class="progress-subline" id="progress-clocks" style="margin-top:12px"></div></div></div><p class="progress-note" id="progress-explanation"></p><p class="table-note">Restored units reduce remaining work without inflating new-work throughput. Unknown totals, warmup, a changed worker count or a stalled pace produce an explicit unavailable estimate. A measured pace range is not a confidence interval or a promise about later phases.</p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/examples/ncaa_review/progress.py">Inspect the executable progress contract ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="section" id="preflight" aria-labelledby="preflight-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Invented portable validation</div><h2 id="preflight-title">Finished checks are not all passes.</h2></div><p>Unsupported optional integration, required capability and unexpected errors have different outcomes. No process, provider or model is accessed by this example.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="demo-buttons" id="preflight-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented preflight scenarios"></div><div class="demo-output" id="preflight-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="coverage-grid" id="preflight-counts"></div><p class="table-note" id="preflight-explanation"></p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/examples/ncaa_review/preflight.py">Inspect the portable validation contract ↗</a></div></section>
    <details class="source-details"><summary>Aggregate provenance and public reproducibility boundary</summary><p>The historical objective and season metrics were independently recomputed from authenticated per-game exports. The public report contains aggregates, calibration bins and descriptive uncertainty. It excludes private data, individual forecasts, feature transforms, active model configurations, weights and execution handoffs. The generic invented example is reproducible here; private real-data retraining is not.</p><p>Accepted historical owner-return SHA-256:<br><span class="hash" id="history-hash"></span></p><p>Latest failed owner-return SHA-256:<br><span class="hash" id="failed-hash"></span></p><p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/tracks/__LEAGUE__/evidence.json">Inspect the exact public aggregate JSON ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/docs/PUBLICATION_BOUNDARY.md">Publication boundary ↗</a></p></details>
